Hollywood, we think of glamour and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.080 --> 00:01:00.580
and action but really it's almost about…it's&nbsp;
like a puppet, we're having our strings pulled.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:06.560
Andy: Absolutely, I mean that's the contract. The&nbsp;
contract we make with the audience is they pay us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.800
money in the form of a box office ticket or in&nbsp;
the form of a paying their cable bill or their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:17.120
streaming app bill and in return we make them&nbsp;
feel something, that's our contract with them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.680
They don't even necessarily know it. If you&nbsp;
ask them they probably wouldn't necessarily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:26.520
describe it (the audience) that way but it is&nbsp;
that. It could be laughter it could be tears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:31.240
it could be being scared, it could be&nbsp;
having your pulse buzzing with excitement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:35.440
it could be getting turned on, but it's&nbsp;
something that makes them feel something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:42.306
that's the relationship between the&nbsp;
filmmaker the screenwriter and the audience.

00:01:42.306 --> 00:01:47.600
